From 0dc9d9b35cabe39fec0a62aef9a4f52bcbfeec3d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nigel Todman <veritas@vts-tech.org>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 15:59:14 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] vkhotkeys

Fix the -vkcapture blue shift and add in-game hotkeys.

- CaptureTGA read back the swapchain with a raw vkCmdCopyImageToBuffer
  (surface-format-native packing) but then unconditionally swapped bytes
  0 and 2 for TGA order. B8G8R8A8 memory is already B,G,R,A - exactly
  TGA's component order - so every capture made on a B8G8R8A8 surface
  (virtually every real platform) came out red/blue flipped. The writer
  now swaps only for R8G8B8A8* surfaces, per the actual chosen format.

- PrintScreen: read back the next presented frame at any moment to the
  first free vkshotNNN.tga (same channel-correct writer as -vkcapture;
  names probed with fopen so nothing is ever overwritten).

- F12: cycle the shader base resolution 1x -> 2x -> 3x -> 4x -> 1x,
  riding the same re-create-and-re-derive path as the F11 aspect toggle.
  The overlay mode row follows immediately and the choice persists via
  shader_base_resolution on exit.

- The overlay grows a short-lived amber feedback row (2 s) for either
  hotkey: 'shot vkshot000.tga' / 'base 640x480 (2x)'.

Both hotkeys are intercepted only while the Vulkan path is active;
-novulkan runs pass the keys to the game unchanged.
